label Greeting
if {Transaction_HasReactiveOpener}:
	ReynaMayari: {Transaction_ReactiveOpener}

if {Transaction_Chapter} == 0.0:
	# Chapter 1 — "Maria From Two Streets Over" (candy | 0 tallies — Comedy & Disguise)
	ReynaMayari: Good day, ordinary merchant. I am merely Maria from two streets over.
	ReynaMayari: Sell me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] from that crystalline sucrose jar. Quickly, please.
	- Welcome, totally normal neighbor Maria.
		ReynaMayari: Excellent. My mortal disguise is completely flawless. Not a soul suspects a thing.
	- Your Majesty, you are literally glowing.
		ReynaMayari: Lower your voice! I have a Council summons in twenty minutes and my robe is doing its best.
	- Sweet tooth acting up, Queen?
		ReynaMayari: Nonsense. Biringan simply lacks affordable mortal confectioneries for my royal research.
	ReynaMayari: Do not mention this visit to your uncle. Just pass over [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color].

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 1.0:
	# Chapter 2 — "Balete Leaves in Sunlight" (frozen / candy | Inflection #1: +1 / +1 / -1 — THE UTANG REVERSAL!)
	ReynaMayari: Back for [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color]. Keep the change, here is a crisp Biringan silver coin.
	ReynaMayari: Wait. Why is it curling up brown? Oh, blast this mortal sunlight.
	ReynaMayari: It turned into a dry balete leaf on your counter. How utterly mortifying.
	ReynaMayari: Listen carefully. I left my mortal pesos in Biringan. Could you put [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] on your lista?
	- Sure. I will list Maria for utang.
		[signal arg="flag:mayari_owes_utang=true"]
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		ReynaMayari: Write Maria, not Her Majesty! Though I admit, having a sari-sari tab feels strangely thrilling.
	- On the house, Your Majesty.
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		ReynaMayari: A queen does not take charity. I will remember this kindness when I deal your next Moon Cards.
	- Cash only. Rules are rules.
		[signal arg="tally:-1"]
		ReynaMayari: Ruthless. Fine, I have crumpled twenty-peso bills from your own ledger tally in my clutch.
	ReynaMayari: Hand over [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] before any neighbor sees that leaf.

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 2.0:
	# Chapter 3 — "The Black Rice Box" (bottle -> allow_sub_cat:candy | Inflection #2: Journal Trapdoor + Substitution!)
	ReynaMayari: No disguise jokes. Biringan's Silver Council caught me tilting your Moon Cards and granting rerolls.
	ReynaMayari: Their Envoy left this black-lacquered box on my doorstep, addressed to Lola's grandchild.
	ReynaMayari: Open it if you wish. Inside is Biringan's finest Black Rice, offered as a "generous buyout" for this shop.
	- No thanks. Black rice binds mortals.
		[signal arg="flag:mayari_refused_black_rice=true"]
		[signal arg="tally:+2"]
		ReynaMayari: Word for word what your Lola told them thirty years ago. You actually read the old lore.
	- Looks fancy. Should I try some?
		ReynaMayari: Hands off that box! One grain and the Silver Council owns your soul forever!
		ReynaMayari: Honestly, mortal, do not scare me like that. I am burning that box myself.
	- Tell the Envoy this shop stays mine.
		[signal arg="flag:mayari_refused_black_rice=true"]
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		ReynaMayari: Good. Never eat a single grain offered by Biringan's Old Houses.
	ReynaMayari: My nerves are frayed. Just sell me plain [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color].
	- [Slide her sweet candy instead.]
		[signal arg="allow_sub_cat:candy"]
		ReynaMayari: Hurry, please. The Envoy is still lurking near the creek bridge.
	- Coming right up, Your Majesty.
		ReynaMayari: Thank you. At least one person on this street keeps their head cool.

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 3.0:
	# Chapter 4 — "The Silver Pact" (snack | Inflection #3: +1 / +1 / -1 — THE REAL TRUTH OF LOLA'S PACT!)
	if {Flag_MayariOwesUtang}:
		ReynaMayari: First, fifteen real mortal pesos. Cross "Maria" off your utang notebook immediately.
	ReynaMayari: You deserve the truth before the Silver Council audits us. Your Lola never owed Biringan a loan.
	ReynaMayari: Decades ago, my Council voted to seal Karimlan's border and pull every spirit away from mortals.
	ReynaMayari: Your Lola marched to the balete gate, refused their Black Rice, and struck the Silver Pact with me instead.
	ReynaMayari: Two thousand pesos in honest mortal coin, proving humans and folklore neighbors still need each other.
	ReynaMayari: Now the Council wants a Charter Trial. How do you plan to answer them, shopkeeper?
	- Let Karimlan speak. Bring the neighbors.
		[signal arg="flag:mayari_trust_barangay=true"]
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		ReynaMayari: Bold. You think this noisy street will actually stand up to Biringan's Old Houses? I hope you are right.
	- Seal the ledger cleanly by their rules.
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		ReynaMayari: Practical and sharp. Even the stiffest aristocrat in Biringan cannot argue with a paid ledger.
	- You should have told me sooner.
		[signal arg="tally:-1"]
		ReynaMayari: Fair. Pride kept my mouth shut until the Envoy knocked.
	ReynaMayari: Sell me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color]. Plotting against my own Council makes me hungry.

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 4.0:
	# Chapter 5 — "The Envoy's Omen" (candy / snack | 0 tallies — Barangay Convergence Payoff!)
	ReynaMayari: The Council's Envoy tried to drop a freezing Omen over Karimlan to make your shop look empty.
	if {Global_CompletedNeighborsCount} >= 3.0:
		ReynaMayari: It failed completely. Your neighbors shoved the mist straight back past the creek!
		if {Flag_BrahimTrueAlbularyo}:
			ReynaMayari: That young albularyo's brass wards were glowing like hearth fires along the road.
		if {Flag_KapQuitSmoking}:
			ReynaMayari: The giant under the acacia just crossed his arms and stared the Envoy down.
		if {Flag_SmkLivingEmblem}:
			ReynaMayari: And that golden rooster puffed its feathers so wide the Envoy nearly tripped into a puddle.
		if {Flag_RosalynAtPeace}:
			ReynaMayari: Even the highway bend stayed warm and calm. I have never seen anything like it.
	else:
		ReynaMayari: Yet your counter stayed open and busy anyway. The Envoy left muttering about stubborn mortals.
	ReynaMayari: Before the Envoy returns to the Silver Spires, they demanded one proof of worth from your counter. What do we send?
	- A bag of humble sari-sari candy.
		ReynaMayari: Let the Silver Council taste real sugar for once. Oh, I am definitely delivering that myself.
	- Exact change and a spotless receipt.
		ReynaMayari: Cold, dignified merchant poise. That will sting their aristocratic pride nicely.
	- Tell them to visit for merienda.
		ReynaMayari: Inviting Biringan's auditors to a wooden bench. Your Lola would have applauded that.
	ReynaMayari: Now pass over [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color]. I earned a snack after that spectacle.

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 5.0:
	# Chapter 6 — "Embassy of the Pale Moon" (candy / frozen | Accumulated Tally Resolution!)
	ReynaMayari: The Silver Council withdrew the audit. Karimlan's border stays open, permanently.
	if {Transaction_Tally} >= 3.0 and ({Flag_MayariRefusedBlackRice} or {Flag_MayariTrustBarangay}):
		[signal arg="outcome:queen_at_the_counter"]
		ReynaMayari: I named your little tindahan an official Embassy of Karimlan. No Old House can touch this street.
		ReynaMayari: Take this Silver Peso of Biringan. I enchanted it myself so sunlight will never turn it into a leaf.
		ReynaMayari: And yes, I am keeping the disguise for daytime candy runs. Less fuss on the street, shopkeeper.
	elif {Transaction_Tally} >= 1.0:
		[signal arg="outcome:honored_charter"]
		ReynaMayari: Lola's Silver Pact stands honored. You proved this counter belongs to both worlds.
		ReynaMayari: Keep my favorite jar stocked, shopkeeper. I am not giving up my daytime errands now.
	else:
		[signal arg="outcome:clean_ledger"]
		ReynaMayari: The Charter holds cleanly by the letter of our agreement. You ran a disciplined shop.
		ReynaMayari: Our business stands settled with full respect.
	ReynaMayari: Now then, real mortal pesos in hand. Sell me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color].

[end_timeline]

label Talk
ReynaMayari: Still waiting on [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color], shopkeeper.
- Out of stock right now, Your Majesty.
	ReynaMayari: Unfortunate. Call your uncle and restock before my next daytime errand.
	[signal arg="refuse_service"]
- Grabbing it right now!
	ReynaMayari: Take your time. I am merely "Maria" browsing the shelves.
[end_timeline]

label Partial
set {Variation} = range(1,4).pick_random()
if {Variation} == 1.0:
	ReynaMayari: Good start. Still missing [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color].
elif {Variation} == 2.0:
	ReynaMayari: That is one part handled. Pass over [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] too.
else:
	ReynaMayari: Almost complete. I still need [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color].
[end_timeline]

label SubstituteItem
[signal arg="tally:+1"]
ReynaMayari: Wait. I asked for water, and you slid me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_SubstituteItemName}[/color].
ReynaMayari: You really think sweet candy solves a political crisis in Biringan?
ReynaMayari: Fine. Keep quiet and let me unwrap one. You are dangerously perceptive, shopkeeper.
[signal arg="story_success"]
[end_timeline]

label Satisfy
if {Transaction_StoryGouged}:
	ReynaMayari: Steep markup for a sovereign in disguise. I will pay it, though I am noting it.
else:
	if {Global_TipActive} == 1.0:
		ReynaMayari: Keep the extra coins. A queen appreciates brisk, discreet service.
	else:
		ReynaMayari: Splendid. Not a word of this visit to Uncle Mario, understood?
[signal arg="story_success"]
[end_timeline]

label WrongItem
ReynaMayari: That is not [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color]. Check the jar again, shopkeeper.
[end_timeline]
